WEBVTT

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.240
What if you could run

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:03.451
a ChatGPT-style app

00:00:03.451 --> 00:00:04.663
on the subscription

00:00:04.663 --> 00:00:05.939
you already pay for?

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:07.944
That is exactly what

00:00:07.944 --> 00:00:09.307
MockChatGPT does.

00:00:09.707 --> 00:00:11.629
It is a familiar chat interface,

00:00:11.629 --> 00:00:12.589
with a genuinely

00:00:12.589 --> 00:00:14.150
agentic engine underneath.

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:16.681
The idea is simple.

00:00:17.081 --> 00:00:18.950
Wrap the OpenAI Codex agent

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:20.542
behind a chat interface

00:00:20.542 --> 00:00:21.719
you already know.

00:00:22.119 --> 00:00:23.426
Because it signs in

00:00:23.426 --> 00:00:24.802
through codex login,

00:00:24.802 --> 00:00:25.903
every turn bills

00:00:25.903 --> 00:00:27.554
to your ChatGPT account.

00:00:27.954 --> 00:00:29.419
There is no API key,

00:00:29.419 --> 00:00:31.177
and no per-token charge.

00:00:31.577 --> 00:00:33.705
Codex ships the hard parts,

00:00:33.705 --> 00:00:35.439
and MockChatGPT builds

00:00:35.439 --> 00:00:37.331
the product around them.

00:00:38.531 --> 00:00:38.956
First,

00:00:38.956 --> 00:00:40.654
the shape of the system.

00:00:41.054 --> 00:00:42.235
There are three layers.

00:00:42.635 --> 00:00:44.418
A vanilla JavaScript app

00:00:44.418 --> 00:00:46.350
talks to an Express server

00:00:46.350 --> 00:00:48.133
over server-sent events.

00:00:48.533 --> 00:00:49.805
The server drives

00:00:49.805 --> 00:00:51.002
the Codex agent,

00:00:51.002 --> 00:00:53.247
running the local codex binary

00:00:53.247 --> 00:00:54.370
against OpenAI.

00:00:54.770 --> 00:00:56.778
State lives in two folders:

00:00:56.778 --> 00:00:58.042
data for records,

00:00:58.042 --> 00:01:00.273
and workspace for the sandbox.

00:01:01.473 --> 00:01:02.279
The server is

00:01:02.279 --> 00:01:03.456
deliberately small.

00:01:03.856 --> 00:01:04.795
Six modules,

00:01:04.795 --> 00:01:07.223
under nine hundred lines total.

00:01:07.623 --> 00:01:09.075
The index module holds

00:01:09.075 --> 00:01:09.801
the routes,

00:01:09.801 --> 00:01:11.253
and the chat endpoint.

00:01:11.653 --> 00:01:13.069
The codex client maps

00:01:13.069 --> 00:01:13.879
agent events

00:01:13.879 --> 00:01:15.632
into simple stream events.

00:01:16.032 --> 00:01:18.385
Prompts builds the persona,

00:01:18.385 --> 00:01:20.998
and store handles persistence.

00:01:21.398 --> 00:01:23.863
A scheduler runs timed tasks,

00:01:23.863 --> 00:01:25.817
and a connectors module

00:01:25.817 --> 00:01:27.771
manages external tools.

00:01:28.971 --> 00:01:29.401
Next,

00:01:29.401 --> 00:01:31.461
follow a single message.

00:01:31.861 --> 00:01:33.487
The browser posts your text

00:01:33.487 --> 00:01:34.993
to the messages endpoint.

00:01:35.393 --> 00:01:37.005
The server saves it,

00:01:37.005 --> 00:01:38.456
builds the prompt,

00:01:38.456 --> 00:01:39.987
and opens a stream.

00:01:40.387 --> 00:01:41.933
It then calls run turn,

00:01:41.933 --> 00:01:44.017
which streams the Codex thread.

00:01:44.417 --> 00:01:45.784
As the agent works,

00:01:45.784 --> 00:01:47.296
each event flows back

00:01:47.296 --> 00:01:48.591
as a stream frame.

00:01:48.991 --> 00:01:50.378
When the turn finishes,

00:01:50.378 --> 00:01:51.524
the reply is saved,

00:01:51.524 --> 00:01:53.031
and a done event is sent.

00:01:54.231 --> 00:01:55.233
Here is a detail

00:01:55.233 --> 00:01:56.047
that matters.

00:01:56.447 --> 00:01:57.779
Codex emits several

00:01:57.779 --> 00:01:59.462
whole messages per turn,

00:01:59.462 --> 00:02:01.074
not token-level deltas.

00:02:01.474 --> 00:02:02.788
So the pipeline

00:02:02.788 --> 00:02:04.276
accumulates them,

00:02:04.276 --> 00:02:05.852
not just the last.

00:02:06.252 --> 00:02:07.992
Every action becomes

00:02:07.992 --> 00:02:09.558
an activity event:

00:02:09.558 --> 00:02:11.298
reasoning, commands,

00:02:11.298 --> 00:02:13.038
searches, and edits.

00:02:13.438 --> 00:02:15.078
The interface replays these

00:02:15.078 --> 00:02:16.778
as a live thinking timeline.

00:02:17.978 --> 00:02:18.973
So what can it

00:02:18.973 --> 00:02:19.825
actually do?

00:02:20.225 --> 00:02:22.295
The familiar ChatGPT surface

00:02:22.295 --> 00:02:23.182
is all here.

00:02:23.582 --> 00:02:25.746
Streaming chat with markdown,

00:02:25.746 --> 00:02:27.685
web search with citations,

00:02:27.685 --> 00:02:29.401
and a code interpreter.

00:02:29.801 --> 00:02:31.620
It understands images,

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:33.026
reads your files,

00:02:33.026 --> 00:02:35.590
and generates images from code.

00:02:35.990 --> 00:02:36.996
The key point:

00:02:36.996 --> 00:02:38.074
one Codex agent

00:02:38.074 --> 00:02:39.296
powers all of it.

00:02:40.496 --> 00:02:41.639
Two research modes

00:02:41.639 --> 00:02:43.290
go beyond a normal answer.

00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:44.260
Wide runs

00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:45.652
a breadth-first sweep.

00:02:46.052 --> 00:02:47.977
At least eight queries,

00:02:47.977 --> 00:02:50.320
and fifteen or more sources.

00:02:50.720 --> 00:02:52.496
Deep goes the other way,

00:02:52.496 --> 00:02:53.975
in iterative rounds.

00:02:54.375 --> 00:02:56.378
It writes notes to a file,

00:02:56.378 --> 00:02:57.611
then chases each

00:02:57.611 --> 00:02:59.537
round's findings further.

00:03:00.737 --> 00:03:02.444
Where does everything persist?

00:03:02.844 --> 00:03:04.466
Each conversation maps

00:03:04.466 --> 00:03:05.941
to one Codex thread,

00:03:05.941 --> 00:03:06.973
resumed by id.

00:03:07.373 --> 00:03:08.966
So context survives

00:03:08.966 --> 00:03:10.392
a server restart.

00:03:10.792 --> 00:03:13.203
Chats, settings, projects,

00:03:13.203 --> 00:03:14.872
and tasks are JSON

00:03:14.872 --> 00:03:15.892
under data.

00:03:16.292 --> 00:03:18.554
Uploads, generated files,

00:03:18.554 --> 00:03:19.459
and memory

00:03:19.459 --> 00:03:21.360
live under workspace.

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:24.163
Connectors extend the agent

00:03:24.163 --> 00:03:25.945
through external tool servers.

00:03:26.345 --> 00:03:28.427
A catalog ships eight picks,

00:03:28.427 --> 00:03:29.542
from Playwright

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:31.251
to document conversion.

00:03:31.651 --> 00:03:33.392
Installs run safely,

00:03:33.392 --> 00:03:35.219
with array arguments,

00:03:35.219 --> 00:03:37.394
never a raw shell string.

00:03:37.794 --> 00:03:39.750
The agent can propose one

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:40.376
in chat,

00:03:40.376 --> 00:03:41.549
and you approve

00:03:41.549 --> 00:03:42.722
with one click.

00:03:43.922 --> 00:03:45.220
Two features make it

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:46.647
feel like a workspace.

00:03:47.047 --> 00:03:48.595
Scheduled tasks run

00:03:48.595 --> 00:03:50.144
on interval, daily,

00:03:50.144 --> 00:03:51.448
weekly, or once.

00:03:51.848 --> 00:03:52.912
Every run is

00:03:52.912 --> 00:03:54.509
a real agent turn,

00:03:54.509 --> 00:03:55.929
in its own chat.

00:03:56.329 --> 00:03:57.533
Projects group chats

00:03:57.533 --> 00:03:58.376
with their own

00:03:58.376 --> 00:03:59.761
instructions and files.

00:04:00.961 --> 00:04:01.302
Now,

00:04:01.302 --> 00:04:03.091
the important caveat.

00:04:03.491 --> 00:04:05.221
This is single-user,

00:04:05.221 --> 00:04:06.865
and localhost-only.

00:04:07.265 --> 00:04:09.261
The agent has write access

00:04:09.261 --> 00:04:10.489
and the network,

00:04:10.489 --> 00:04:12.101
and there is no auth.

00:04:12.501 --> 00:04:13.732
Exposing the port

00:04:13.732 --> 00:04:15.253
would hand a stranger

00:04:15.253 --> 00:04:16.774
control of the agent.

00:04:17.174 --> 00:04:18.798
File names and ids

00:04:18.798 --> 00:04:20.062
are validated,

00:04:20.062 --> 00:04:22.409
and markdown is sanitized.

00:04:23.609 --> 00:04:24.746
The whole project

00:04:24.746 --> 00:04:26.218
is remarkably compact.

00:04:26.618 --> 00:04:28.744
About 3,200 lines,

00:04:28.744 --> 00:04:30.751
six dependencies,

00:04:30.751 --> 00:04:32.523
and zero tests.

00:04:32.923 --> 00:04:34.714
Built in a single day,

00:04:34.714 --> 00:04:36.424
across seven commits.

00:04:36.824 --> 00:04:39.924
The frontend is one script,

00:04:39.924 --> 00:04:41.072
965 lines,

00:04:41.072 --> 00:04:42.565
no framework.

00:04:43.765 --> 00:04:44.740
So remember it

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:45.367
this way.

00:04:45.767 --> 00:04:48.396
A full ChatGPT-style product,

00:04:48.396 --> 00:04:51.296
wrapped around the Codex engine.

00:04:51.696 --> 00:04:53.229
A thin server,

00:04:53.229 --> 00:04:54.982
a lean frontend,

00:04:54.982 --> 00:04:57.391
and a sandboxed agent.

00:04:57.791 --> 00:04:59.147
All on the subscription

00:04:59.147 --> 00:05:00.149
you already have.
